From 308f005c0d63ff521553d45b58c7bb7c3d895d86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:05:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] viewer2: fascia R rev B on the page (upright J1, the rev
 B zip, the case 2.8 mm lower)

The build failed as it stood: the case model now draws the lead only for the
upright J1, and order.py named the rev A zip. assembly.py gives the case model
R's upright J1 (use_fascia_j1, also for A and W); order.py orders
fab/TS06-FASCIA-R-revB-divider-holes04-fab.zip and checks ORDER.md's rev B
paragraph. The page: the lead rises in a gentle S into an upright housing,
the Order view's rev B card, the case 2.8 mm lower, texts. Tests for the rev B
zip and the upright lead end. Built clean (30.9 MB, 101 files); the suite was
not run (the page update is on hold).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WoV3gyAFgmtuk6W6Dr4bdA
